ohan20/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/khuranarohan20/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/khuranarohan20","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khuranarohan20/knky-chat/commits/7d977b8a98182e95cdd726208d107b1ed8ec94cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-06T13:31:41Z","email":"rohan.khurana.dev.iic@gmail.com","name":"Rohan Khurana"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-06T13:31:41Z","email":"rohan.khurana.dev.iic@gmail.com","name":"Rohan Khurana"},"message":"feat: create adapter layer for platform integration\n\nAdapters package now contains:\n- Platform adapter interfaces and types\n- Core adapter (Next.js + Bootstrap, single creator)\n- Agency adapter (React + Vite + Tailwind, multi-creator)\n- Theme abstraction and CSS variable management\n\nKey features:\n- Abstract IPlatformAdapter interface for platform flexibility\n- CoreAdapter for single-creator flat state structure\n- AgencyAdapter for multi-creator nested state with creator isolation\n- Creator switching support for agency platform\n- Theme management (Bootstrap/Tailwind CSS variables)\n- Authentication integration hooks\n- Socket connection lifecycle management\n- Message handling and state synchronization\n\nPlatform-specific adapters abstract differences between:\n- State structures (flat vs nested)\n- Authentication (single vs per-creator tokens)\n- UI frameworks (Bootstrap vs Tailwind)\n- Environment variables (process.env vs import.meta.env)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c451c2ec17579fd00739c725575dc3e3dc926c26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khuranarohan20/knky-chat/git/trees/c451c2ec17579fd00739c725575dc3e3dc926c26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/khuranarohan20/knky-chat/git/commits/7d977b8a98182e95cdd726208d107b1ed8ec94cb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_a