b.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/c4fd9a311a472f764a18ef624f1dbf1f947ec198"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/9ec4229b0403cb907f75c95f40ce09ad55cfc39d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:45:56Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:45:56Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Speak to the reviewer by default, to the engineer on request\n\nThe person leaving comments is usually not an engineer; the person\nacting on them usually is. The toolbar now follows the pattern design\ntools use for that split: plain language everywhere by default, and one\nremembered switch that turns on the engineering layer.\n\n- every anchor captures a display label from the component name, the\n  node''s visible text and the section heading it sits under, so a\n  comment is on \"Status badge \"Failed\" in Payments\", not on a path\n- only trouble gets a status (\"Best match\", \"Not in this build\"); a\n  comment that is where it was left shows none\n- Technical details, in the panel header and remembered per reviewer,\n  reveals paths, source refs, anchor levels, the lock and its diff, the\n  orphan rate, re-anchoring, and the Network, Runtime and Build views;\n  each comment also has its own Details disclosure\n- the Send view lists what will go in the reviewer''s words, with the\n  exact packet one click away; the digest prints the label first\n- copy: Comment on something, Comments (n), Include when sent, Close\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"3377acc7a8a237f9758f6c75ae167850ce154dd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/3377acc7a8a237f9758f6c75ae167850ce154dd3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/9ec4229b0403cb907f75c95f40ce09ad55cfc39d","verification":{"payload":"tree 3377acc7a8a237f9758f6c75ae167850ce154dd3\nparent 87543a8302abb6eafecea93a5110d264543f3d70\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789242356 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789242356 +0000\n\nSpeak to the reviewer by default, to the engineer on request\n\nThe person leaving comments is usually not an engineer; the person\nacting on them usually is. The toolbar now follows the pattern design\ntools use for that split: plain language everywhere by default, and one\nremembered switch that turns on the engineering layer.\n\n- every anchor captures a display label from the component name, the\n  node''s visible text and the section heading it sits under, so a\n  comment is on \"Status badge \"Failed\" in Payments\", not on a path\n- only trouble gets a status (\"Best match\", \"Not in this build\"); a\n  comment that is where it was left shows none\n- Technical details, in the panel header and remembered per reviewer,\n  reveals paths, source refs, anchor levels, the lock and its diff, the\n  orphan rate, re-anchoring, and the Network, Runtime and Build views;\n  each comment also has its own Details disclosure\n- the Send view lists what will go in the reviewer''s words, with the\n  exact packet one click away; the digest prints the label first\n- copy: Comment on something, Comments (n), Include when sent, Close\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPOOtu2L\n8ew2VhC6wdgnVSz+ZW4wrVKkFCHNE+ePi9RDT3VTqBaNyXHmOkvbnKM9CUu39kWElmxF+JJYmD3X\ntQo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/9ec4229b0403cb907f75c95f40ce09ad55cfc39d","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDllYzQyMjliMDQwM2NiOTA3Zjc1Yzk1ZjQwY2UwOWFkNTVjZmMzOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/87543a8302abb6eafecea93a5110d264543f3d70","sha":"87543a8302abb6eafecea93a5110d264543f3d70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/87543a8302abb6eafecea93a5110d264543f3d70"}],"sha":"9ec4229b0403cb907f75c95f40ce09ad55cfc39d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/9ec4229b0403cb907f75c95f40ce09ad55cfc39d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/87543a8302abb6eafecea93a5110d264543f3d70/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:33:27Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T19:33:27Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Count each thread once per build in the orphan meter\n\nA federated preview can be measured before its last remote has painted.\nThe meter appended a sample per pass, so an early reading of a\nhalf-rendered page sat in the average for good and the rate crept\n(1/2, 2/3, 3/4...) as later passes corrected the anchors but not the\nnumber. Now a metered pass replaces a thread''s sample for that build,\nso the build''s rate is what the last look said.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"9c7b1347f3c01eb510613249efca674baa1fd3d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/9c7b1347f3c01eb510613249efca674baa1fd3d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/87543a8302abb6eafecea93a5110d264543f3d70","verification":{"payload":"tree 9c7b1347f3c01eb510613249efca674baa1fd3d9\nparent e670963d0c3fdceb2d236dc0f02957aa9ce9ff16\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789241607 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789241607 +0000\n\nCount each thread once per build in the orphan meter\n\nA federated preview can be measured before its last remote has painted.\nThe meter appended a sample per pass, so an early reading of a\nhalf-rendered page sat in the average for good and the rate crept\n(1/2, 2/3, 3/4...) as later passes corrected the anchors but not the\nnumber. Now a metered pass replaces a thread''s sample for that build,\nso the build''s rate is what the last look said.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPDX7kFW\nH5weX/OLa7/468BNYrMFslldAOQW/XQ8BZQ68PplIOBzC1banh8obUjjSFpkL6X9FU5l7Uyg3vWE\nZgA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/87543a8302abb6eafecea93a5110d264543f3d70","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDg3NTQzYTgzMDJhYmI2ZWFmZWNlYTkzYTUxMTBkMjY0NTQzZjNkNzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/e670963d0c3fdceb2d236dc0f02957aa9ce9ff16","sha":"e670963d0c3fdceb2d236dc0f02957aa9ce9ff16","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/e670963d0c3fdceb2d236dc0f02957aa9ce9ff16"}],"sha":"87543a8302abb6eafecea93a5110d264543f3d70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/87543a8302abb6eafecea93a5110d264543f3d70"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/e670963d0c3fdceb2d236dc0f02957aa9ce9ff16/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T03:19:09Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T03:19:09Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Let the reviewer choose what the agent gets, and say it as text\n\nThe previous submission path sent every thread regardless of the tick\nboxes, and general feedback was a runtime-event in disguise with a\ncheckbox that did nothing. Now:\n\n- a thread is in the next submission when it is open and the reviewer\n  has not unticked \"send to agent\"; closed threads never are\n- general feedback is its own anchor kind with a topic, composed from\n  the dock like an element comment, with no pin because it has no node\n- the Submit tab shows the packet as a digest before it goes: element\n  feedback first with its location, then preview-wide feedback, then\n  network, runtime and build\n- the host receives a FeedbackSubmission through onSubmit; the shell\n  records it in localStorage and prints the digest, since Phase 1 has\n  no agent behind the toolbar\n- pins and cards share one numbering, by creation order\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"b4163e847f27eb4d3c9ebeb365f728723ac2c89f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/b4163e847f27eb4d3c9ebeb365f728723ac2c89f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/e670963d0c3fdceb2d236dc0f02957aa9ce9ff16","verification":{"payload":"tree b4163e847f27eb4d3c9ebeb365f728723ac2c89f\nparent bcc3c79a10f45a9a5d9fa16c39d3dd99b6da415e\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789183149 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789183149 +0000\n\nLet the reviewer choose what the agent gets, and say it as text\n\nThe previous submission path sent every thread regardless of the tick\nboxes, and general feedback was a runtime-event in disguise with a\ncheckbox that did nothing. Now:\n\n- a thread is in the next submission when it is open and the reviewer\n  has not unticked \"send to agent\"; closed threads never are\n- general feedback is its own anchor kind with a topic, composed from\n  the dock like an element comment, with no pin because it has no node\n- the Submit tab shows the packet as a digest before it goes: element\n  feedback first with its location, then preview-wide feedback, then\n  network, runtime and build\n- the host receives a FeedbackSubmission through onSubmit; the shell\n  records it in localStorage and prints the digest, since Phase 1 has\n  no agent behind the toolbar\n- pins and cards share one numbering, by creation order\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----