actoring to Figma-style feedback\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJHR23jK\n1dGLoUOvodQESZIPxbToGOwUmzQUu/Fwahx+3fmdAETCwho0KpptO9c+dhGQBys7DkRieYu1sNX/\nNA8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/a04d9ee014377aaeb255e96e9e6ab6a0e514a0ed","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKGEwNGQ5ZWUwMTQzNzdhYWViMjU1ZTk2ZTllNmFiNmEwZTUxNGEwZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/3b87127dc70e62b4a826d37a665a1199e4e0fb73","sha":"3b87127dc70e62b4a826d37a665a1199e4e0fb73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/3b87127dc70e62b4a826d37a665a1199e4e0fb73"}],"sha":"a04d9ee014377aaeb255e96e9e6ab6a0e514a0ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/a04d9ee014377aaeb255e96e9e6ab6a0e514a0ed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/3b87127dc70e62b4a826d37a665a1199e4e0fb73/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T03:00:34Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T03:00:34Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Refactor to Figma-style inline feedback with submission workflow\n\nAdd support for:\n1. Figma-style inline comment annotations (pins show at elements)\n2. Free-form general feedback not tied to specific elements\n3. Comment selection/filtering for submission\n4. Submission workflow with summary and preview\n5. All visual comments now show pins (not just open ones), with resolved comments faded\n\nNew features:\n- toggleThreadSelection(): track which comments are included in submission\n- addGeneralFeedback(): add comments not tied to elements\n- GeneralFeedbackTab: compose and view general feedback\n- SubmissionTab: review selected comments, summary, and submit to agent\n- Updated FeedbackLayer to show pins for all visual threads with thread status\n- Enhanced ThreadCard with checkbox to select for submission\n\nThe toolbar now supports the full Figma-like workflow:\n- Click element -> comment form appears inline\n- Add general feedback about patterns, spacing, etc.\n- Review and select which comments to include\n- Submit selected comments to agent for processing","tree":{"sha":"c744935aa629777bdb6efd303efda6633c8b8df2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/c744935aa629777bdb6efd303efda6633c8b8df2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/3b87127dc70e62b4a826d37a665a1199e4e0fb73","verification":{"payload":"tree c744935aa629777bdb6efd303efda6633c8b8df2\nparent ea99fbbe6d6ac009980f5cb5dce9ad8227da1886\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789182034 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789182034 +0000\n\nRefactor to Figma-style inline feedback with submission workflow\n\nAdd support for:\n1. Figma-style inline comment annotations (pins show at elements)\n2. Free-form general feedback not tied to specific elements\n3. Comment selection/filtering for submission\n4. Submission workflow with summary and preview\n5. All visual comments now show pins (not just open ones), with resolved comments faded\n\nNew features:\n- toggleThreadSelection(): track which comments are included in submission\n- addGeneralFeedback(): add comments not tied to elements\n- GeneralFeedbackTab: compose and view general feedback\n- SubmissionTab: review selected comments, summary, and submit to agent\n- Updated FeedbackLayer to show pins for all visual threads with thread status\n- Enhanced ThreadCard with checkbox to select for submission\n\nThe toolbar now supports the full Figma-like workflow:\n- Click element -> comment form appears inline\n- Add general feedback about patterns, spacing, etc.\n- Review and select which comments to include\n- Submit selected comments to agent for processing\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMUbGJrf\nfqFAPeQiTsl40y7mauVuiJ9UE8P/nxE5Bzo6YAW1uTmdb1CIm9nvEj+/RrKRNJje6r5gqrQ8T85R\nNQw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/3b87127dc70e62b4a826d37a665a1199e4e0fb73","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDNiODcxMjdkYzcwZTYyYjRhODI2ZDM3YTY2NWExMTk5ZTRlMGZiNzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/ea99fbbe6d6ac009980f5cb5dce9ad8227da1886","sha":"ea99fbbe6d6ac009980f5cb5dce9ad8227da1886","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/ea99fbbe6d6ac009980f5cb5dce9ad8227da1886"}],"sha":"3b87127dc70e62b4a826d37a665a1199e4e0fb73","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/3b87127dc70e62b4a826d37a665a1199e4e0fb73"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/ea99fbbe6d6ac009980f5cb5dce9ad8227da1886/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T02:28:27Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T02:28:27Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Make one remote a Webpack build and keep the toolbar out of the design system\n\nThree corrections to the phase 1 fixtures, and the production leaks they\nuncovered.\n\nOne remote is now built with Webpack and @module-federation/enhanced, because\nthat is what many teams use. apps/limits-mfe emits a module-type remote entry\nthat the Vite host consumes exactly like its Vite remote, and the host resolves\nan element inside it through the same identity chain: both adapters share one\nanalysis pass, so the bundler does not change what anything is called.\n\nThe toolbar is no longer a Salt consumer. The application and the shell are Salt\nand run under a SaltProvider; the toolbar is the tool looking at them. Building\nit from the same components made \"this button is wrong\" ambiguous about which\nbutton, put a second SaltProvider in the page, and tied the review layer''s\nrelease to the application''s design-system version. It now styles itself from\nthe Frame''s tokens with literal fallbacks, so it follows a Salt theme when there\nis one and still renders when there is not.\n\nFeedback on a Salt application is about Salt decisions, so the fixtures give a\nreviewer something real to say: status reads through StatusIndicator sentiment\nrather than a colour, and the manifest records the design-system props an author\nset plus the provider mode and density in force, so \"a failed settlement is an\nerror, not a caution\" resolves to a component and a prop rather than to a pixel.\n\nTwo production leaks fell out of the rework, both now closed and covered:\n\n- The Webpack loader passed source straight through when instrumentation was\n  off, so authored data-de-instance-key attributes reached the artifact. The\n  pass now runs either way and strips instead of injecting.\n- The shell imported the review layer statically, so a production build carried\n  the whole toolbar. The review layer moved behind one dynamic import that only\n  a preview build reaches, and the application publishes the pinned build over a\n  bridge that imports nothing.\n\npnpm verify:production now passes for all three apps by inspection of the\nartifacts. 88 unit tests, 16 browser tests, 29 requirements traced.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"2b94ce9e8e2d1bc5ae39005da265595b6f66677c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/2b94ce9e8e2d1bc5ae39005da265595b6f66677c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/ea99fbbe6d6ac009980f5cb5dce9ad8227da1886","verification":{"payload":"tree 2b94ce9e8e2d1bc5ae39005da265595b6f66677c\nparent 2fd4936fe73123096e8f1ec6d23bbc72b29ab2f6\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789180107 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789180107 +0000\n\nMake one remote a Webpack build and keep the toolbar out of the design system\n\nThree corrections to the phase 1 fixtures, and the production leaks they\nuncovered.\n\nOne remote is now built with Webpack and @module-federation/enhanced, because\nthat is what many teams use. apps/limits-mfe emits a module-type remote entry\nthat the Vite host consumes exactly like its Vite remote, and the host resolves\nan element inside it through the same identity chain: both adapters share one\nanalysis pass, so the bundler does not change what anything is called.\n\nThe toolbar is no longer a Salt consumer. The application and the shell are Salt\nand run under a SaltProvider; the toolbar is the tool looking at them. Building\nit from the same components made \"this button is wrong\" ambiguous about which\nbutton, put a second SaltProvider in the page, and tied the review layer''s\nrelease to the application''s design-system version. It now styles itself from\nthe Frame''s tokens with literal fallbacks, so it follows a Salt theme when there\nis one and still renders when there is not.\n\nFeedback on a Salt application is about Salt decisions, so the fixtures give a\nreviewer something real to say: status reads through StatusIndicator sentiment\nrather than a colour, and the manifest records the design-system props an author\nset plus the provider mode and density in force, so \"a failed settlement is an\nerror, not a caution\" resolves to a component and a prop rather than to a pixel.\n\nTwo production leaks fell out of the rework, both now closed and covered:\n\n- The Webpack loader passed source straight through when instrumentation was\n  off, so authored data-de-instance-key attributes reached the artifact. The\n  pass now runs either way and strips instead of injecting.\n- The shell imported the review layer statically, so a production build carried\n  the whole toolbar. The review layer moved behind one dynamic import that only\n  a preview build reaches, and the application publishes the pinned build over a\n  bridge that imports nothing.\n\npnpm verify:production now passes for all three apps by inspection of the\nartifacts. 88 unit tests, 16 browser tests, 29 requirements traced.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ2d/u39\njTcScjvh8SmdlPt1eltqjGbKy5aQT+ZwRv2mlLfYQjkaafjIaebFT4sykLqDtwy5tuOQjQdCN5lj\nuQo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/ea99fbbe6d6ac009980f5cb5dce9ad8227da1886","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKGVhOTlmYmJlNmQ2YWMwMDk5ODBmNWNiNWRjZTlhZDgyMjdkYTE4ODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/2fd4936fe73123096e8f1ec6d23bbc72b29ab2f6","sha":"2fd4936fe73123096e8f1ec6d23bbc72b29ab2f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/2fd4936fe73123096e8f1ec6d23bbc72b29ab2f6"}],"sha":"ea99fbbe6d6ac009980f5cb5dce9ad8227da1886","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/ea99fbbe6d6ac009980f5cb5dce9ad8227da1886"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/2fd4936fe73123096e8f1ec6d23bbc72b29ab2f6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T01:44:19Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T01:44:19Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Document the instrumenter\n\nInstallation, architecture and troubleshooting for @de/ui-provenance, and a\nroot README that now points at it for the first level of the anchor chain.\n\nThe architecture notes are explicit about what is deliberately excluded from\nthe fingerprint and why, because every exclusion is a decision someone will\notherwise re-litigate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"2eb4e86b662a2b457f59e1ab1c12d9b5704e3bfa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/2eb4e86b662a2b457f59e1ab1c12d9b5704e3bfa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/2fd4936fe73123096e8f1ec6d23bbc72b29ab2f6","verification":{"payload":"tree 2eb4e86b662a2b457f59e1ab1c12d9b5704e3bfa\nparent a62aebd2a553f5aa20cdbfcdaad1848c8186271a\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789177459 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789177459 +0000\n\nDocument the instrumenter\n\nInstallation, architecture and troubleshooting for @de/ui-provenance, and a\nroot README that now points at it for the first level of the anchor chain.\n\nThe architecture notes are explicit about what is deliberately excluded from\nthe fingerprint and why, because every exclusion is a decision someone will\notherwise re-litigate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH7rrAEi\nKFMn4Jf+KLJNg1tJ+Wr8mSf4sBmDotgncibn662YjzmcNRw+vPPmkQDmmGgdOvgPfF8schRj+qyG\nSQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/2fd4936fe73123096e8f1ec6d23bbc72b29ab2f6","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDJmZDQ5MzZmZTczMTIzMDk2ZThmMWVjNmQyM2JiYzcyYjI5YWIyZjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/a62aebd2a553f5aa20cdbfcdaad1848c8186271a","sha":"a62aebd2a553f5aa20cdbfcdaad1848c8186271a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/a62aebd2a553f5aa20cdbfcdaad1848c8186271a"}],"sha":"2fd4936fe73123096e8f1ec6d23bbc72b29ab2f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/2fd4936fe73123096e8f1ec6d23bbc72b29ab2f6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/a62aebd2a553f5aa20cdbfcdaad1848c8186271a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T01:44:19Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T01:44:19Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Move the feedback toolbar onto registry-backed identity\n\nThe toolbar''s provenance level was matching on a module, line and column token,\nwhich is exactly the identity the instrumenter exists to replace. It now reads\nthe instrumenter''s source ids, and the old @adl/provenance package is retired\nrather than left as a second instrumenter nobody should use.\n\nThe tests change with it, and the changes are the point: a comment that\nsurvived a file move as \"degraded, 0.80\" now survives it exactly, because the\nregistry carried its id across. Staleness stays separate from anchoring - the\npinned inputs still moved, and the thread still says so.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"5184b2b4ce067577010bcdf85b766540a3786651","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/5184b2b4ce067577010bcdf85b766540a3786651"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/a62aebd2a553f5aa20cdbfcdaad1848c8186271a","verification":{"payload":"tree 5184b2b4ce067577010bcdf85b766540a3786651\nparent 8842001cab3fb2c84769ae47ac19072aec25b639\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789177459 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789177459 +0000\n\nMove the feedback toolbar onto registry-backed identity\n\nThe toolbar''s provenance level was matching on a module, line and column token,\nwhich is exactly the identity the instrumenter exists to replace. It now reads\nthe instrumenter''s source ids, and the old @adl/provenance package is retired\nrather than left as a second instrumenter nobody should use.\n\nThe tests change with it, and the changes are the point: a comment that\nsurvived a file move as \"degraded, 0.80\" now survives it exactly, because the\nregistry carried its id across. Staleness stays separate from anchoring - the\npinned inputs still moved, and the thread still says so.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMQhhZSM\nt94o9kUoXh2PF4f68NCZ6d1N9leSj4nAa+qpODV7M7ZEpQ3yw1MtLspuV5GjonTVb3eZgPmbxKyd\nPwM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE----