":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/8842001cab3fb2c84769ae47ac19072aec25b639/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T01:44:18Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T01:44:18Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Instrument the fixtures and add a Preview Review Layer fixture\n\nThe host and both remotes now carry committed registries and publish their own\nmanifests. The fixtures grew the cases the browser suite needs and a single\nbundle cannot fake: a Salt dialog rendered through a portal, an open shadow\nroot, and an iframe.\n\nThe review fixture is the minimum consumer of the contract - select an element,\nshow what the runtime resolved it to. It owns no comments and no storage, and\nit is dynamically imported behind a statically dead branch so production never\ncarries it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"6f2573326fb89f50c4298a5d8a011fea51bd00cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/6f2573326fb89f50c4298a5d8a011fea51bd00cd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/8842001cab3fb2c84769ae47ac19072aec25b639","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f2573326fb89f50c4298a5d8a011fea51bd00cd\nparent 46b429385f3ff137faa266f4bf6c78f8ebc6e33b\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789177458 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789177458 +0000\n\nInstrument the fixtures and add a Preview Review Layer fixture\n\nThe host and both remotes now carry committed registries and publish their own\nmanifests. The fixtures grew the cases the browser suite needs and a single\nbundle cannot fake: a Salt dialog rendered through a portal, an open shadow\nroot, and an iframe.\n\nThe review fixture is the minimum consumer of the contract - select an element,\nshow what the runtime resolved it to. It owns no comments and no storage, and\nit is dynamically imported behind a statically dead branch so production never\ncarries it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNhf/dZT\nHnQQkJItLbxnvIAopwQTL/0ZC03Nmkx/J2kvduOoda3PnHA6Vk67rbBMXAu5dl6XAtRK6kOIjB0m\nQwY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/8842001cab3fb2c84769ae47ac19072aec25b639","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDg4NDIwMDFjYWIzZmIyYzg0NzY5YWU0N2FjMTkwNzJhZWMyNWI2Mzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/46b429385f3ff137faa266f4bf6c78f8ebc6e33b","sha":"46b429385f3ff137faa266f4bf6c78f8ebc6e33b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/46b429385f3ff137faa266f4bf6c78f8ebc6e33b"}],"sha":"8842001cab3fb2c84769ae47ac19072aec25b639","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/8842001cab3fb2c84769ae47ac19072aec25b639"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/46b429385f3ff137faa266f4bf6c78f8ebc6e33b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T01:44:18Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T01:44:18Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Prove stability, Salt compatibility and production exclusion\n\nThe specification puts identity before the toolbar, and this is the evidence\nthat it holds.\n\nThe golden evaluation applies a twelve-edit suite to a 151-element fixture and\nreports retention and false reattachment as machine-readable output: 100% for\nformatting-only edits, 100% across the ordinary suite including file moves,\ncomponent renames and subtree wrapping, and zero false reattachments. Zero\nfalse reattachments takes precedence over retention, so it is asserted first.\n\nThe Salt catalog is generated by rendering each required component in a real\nbrowser and asking the DOM what became of the attribute. A TypeScript prop\ndefinition is not evidence; all nine forward it to exactly one node, and only\nthat classification is injected into.\n\nProduction exclusion is proven by inspecting the artifact, not by trusting the\nflag. Doing so found three real leaks: authored keys shipping in application\nsource, the federation runtime plugin baked into the host bundle, and a\npreview-only chunk that survived because its dynamic import was not statically\ndead. All three are fixed; the check now also asserts that a production build\nwhich is asked for instrumentation refuses.\n\nBoth measured budgets are recorded: 6.9% preview build overhead against 15%,\nand 0.2ms p95 resolution against one animation frame.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"9deea35c98d8faee9cbb873b137ae1c74e3b7f01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/9deea35c98d8faee9cbb873b137ae1c74e3b7f01"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/46b429385f3ff137faa266f4bf6c78f8ebc6e33b","verification":{"payload":"tree 9deea35c98d8faee9cbb873b137ae1c74e3b7f01\nparent f44ee3990068af3d88151ea7f455b7dbada8adcd\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789177458 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789177458 +0000\n\nProve stability, Salt compatibility and production exclusion\n\nThe specification puts identity before the toolbar, and this is the evidence\nthat it holds.\n\nThe golden evaluation applies a twelve-edit suite to a 151-element fixture and\nreports retention and false reattachment as machine-readable output: 100% for\nformatting-only edits, 100% across the ordinary suite including file moves,\ncomponent renames and subtree wrapping, and zero false reattachments. Zero\nfalse reattachments takes precedence over retention, so it is asserted first.\n\nThe Salt catalog is generated by rendering each required component in a real\nbrowser and asking the DOM what became of the attribute. A TypeScript prop\ndefinition is not evidence; all nine forward it to exactly one node, and only\nthat classification is injected into.\n\nProduction exclusion is proven by inspecting the artifact, not by trusting the\nflag. Doing so found three real leaks: authored keys shipping in application\nsource, the federation runtime plugin baked into the host bundle, and a\npreview-only chunk that survived because its dynamic import was not statically\ndead. All three are fixed; the check now also asserts that a production build\nwhich is asked for instrumentation refuses.\n\nBoth measured budgets are recorded: 6.9% preview build overhead against 15%,\nand 0.2ms p95 resolution against one animation frame.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFM/XTyb\nUO6gD7w7j0p4T6xjgFyd30F4FPJz+uJkbhKzzjbpo9iceF2KE3vEHgOZsRniqUg7wJzg+e8rr+1s\nZws=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/46b429385f3ff137faa266f4bf6c78f8ebc6e33b","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDQ2YjQyOTM4NWYzZmYxMzdmYWEyNjZmNGJmNmM3OGY4ZWJjNmUzM2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/f44ee3990068af3d88151ea7f455b7dbada8adcd","sha":"f44ee3990068af3d88151ea7f455b7dbada8adcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/f44ee3990068af3d88151ea7f455b7dbada8adcd"}],"sha":"46b429385f3ff137faa266f4bf6c78f8ebc6e33b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/46b429385f3ff137faa266f4bf6c78f8ebc6e33b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/f44ee3990068af3d88151ea7f455b7dbada8adcd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T01:43:55Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T01:43:55Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Add the runtime resolution SDK and the source-time lint rules\n\nOwnership resolves attribute first, mount root last. A host''s root encloses\nevery remote on the page, so trusting it first would attribute a remote''s\nelement to the shell - and a Salt dialog rendered through a portal sits outside\nevery root while still belonging to the remote that rendered it.\n\nConfidence is decided in one place, because the difference between strong and\nweak is the difference between showing a reviewer their comment reattached and\nasking them first. \"The element left the build\" stays distinct from \"it exists\nbut is not on this screen\": the first is triage, the second is a route change.\n\nAnchors carry hashes, never the visible text, since an anchor may travel\nfurther than the screen it came from. WebCrypto is unavailable outside a secure\ncontext, so there is a fallback - neither path is a security boundary; both\nexist so raw copy does not travel.\n\nOpen shadow boundaries are crossed. An iframe, or a custom element exposing no\nopen root, returns UIP_UNSUPPORTED_BOUNDARY rather than guessing at the host.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"8415f8487a335b567cfdb7d8e39fe3965ebcb04a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/8415f8487a335b567cfdb7d8e39fe3965ebcb04a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/f44ee3990068af3d88151ea7f455b7dbada8adcd","verification":{"payload":"tree 8415f8487a335b567cfdb7d8e39fe3965ebcb04a\nparent 6061f26804a09e09db508ae74c98abeaa91aae02\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789177435 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789177435 +0000\n\nAdd the runtime resolution SDK and the source-time lint rules\n\nOwnership resolves attribute first, mount root last. A host''s root encloses\nevery remote on the page, so trusting it first would attribute a remote''s\nelement to the shell - and a Salt dialog rendered through a portal sits outside\nevery root while still belonging to the remote that rendered it.\n\nConfidence is decided in one place, because the difference between strong and\nweak is the difference between showing a reviewer their comment reattached and\nasking them first. \"The element left the build\" stays distinct from \"it exists\nbut is not on this screen\": the first is triage, the second is a route change.\n\nAnchors carry hashes, never the visible text, since an anchor may travel\nfurther than the screen it came from. WebCrypto is unavailable outside a secure\ncontext, so there is a fallback - neither path is a security boundary; both\nexist so raw copy does not travel.\n\nOpen shadow boundaries are crossed. An iframe, or a custom element exposing no\nopen root, returns UIP_UNSUPPORTED_BOUNDARY rather than guessing at the host.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDCsORqn\noU0hsFz7tvFbffKEK8pqcDswMedqgYh59DV5bgJXb6dtJJdJ+Ue5Iq/Ukqfq5IVJE9AyTL+ad/90\n3A8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/f44ee3990068af3d88151ea7f455b7dbada8adcd","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKGY0NGVlMzk5MDA2OGFmM2Q4ODE1MWVhN2Y0NTViN2RiYWRhOGFkY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/6061f26804a09e09db508ae74c98abeaa91aae02","sha":"6061f26804a09e09db508ae74c98abeaa91aae02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/6061f26804a09e09db508ae74c98abeaa91aae02"}],"sha":"f44ee3990068af3d88151ea7f455b7dbada8adcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/f44ee3990068af3d88151ea7f455b7dbada8adcd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/6061f26804a09e09db508ae74c98abeaa91aae02/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T01:43:55Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T01:43:55Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Add the Vite, Webpack and Module Federation adapters\n\nOne analysis pass, shared: identity is decided once so a Vite build and a\nWebpack build of the same source cannot disagree about what anything is called.\n\nVite injects through the host''s existing JSX pass rather than regenerating\nmodules. Regenerating works in isolation, but it hands other plugins a module\nthey did not produce, and the federation plugin duly mistook an ordinary\ncomponent for an application entry. Webpack runs the same transform through a\nloader, with the plugin and loader meeting on the prepared project.\n\nRemotes register through documented Module Federation 2 runtime lifecycle\nhooks, never through a federation debugging global. Identity comes from each\nremote''s own manifest rather than its federation name, because remote names\nrepeat across environments and the application id is firm-controlled.\n\nInstrumentation is off unless DE_UI_PROVENANCE_ENABLED is set, and a production\nbuild refuses it outright.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"4b3fb7f259c639755136a4ca11888a4dabd33503","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/4b3fb7f259c639755136a4ca11888a4dabd33503"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/6061f26804a09e09db508ae74c98abeaa91aae02","verification":{"payload":"tree 4b3fb7f259c639755136a4ca11888a4dabd33503\nparent c492ba22f3cfab47ddd322b51e6d8481baf4053f\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789177435 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789177435 +0000\n\nAdd the Vite, Webpack and Module Federation adapters\n\nOne analysis pass, shared: identity is decided once so a Vite build and a\nWebpack build of the same source cannot disagree about what anything is called.\n\nVite injects through the host''s existing JSX pass rather than regenerating\nmodules. Regenerating works in isolation, but it hands other plugins a module\nthey did not produce, and the federation plugin duly mistook an ordinary\ncomponent for an application entry. Webpack runs the same transform through a\nloader, with the plugin and loader meeting on the prepared project.\n\nRemotes register through documented Module Federation 2 runtime lifecycle\nhooks, never through a federation debugging global. Identity comes from each\nremote''s own manifest rather than its federation name, because remote names\nrepeat across environments and the application id is firm-controlled.\n\nInstrumentation is off unless DE_UI_PROVENANCE_ENABLED is set, and a production\nbuild refuses it outright.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAX4u4Qn\nL/eRA/r0r5YV6eftm3DsfofUKFSPJqKBjEIEYU/m2Y70+ii9RoZxPf7MFpJv3lhjfkfG1usff76A\nuws=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/6061f26804a09e09db508ae74c98abeaa91aae02","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDYwNjFmMjY4MDRhMDllMDlkYjUwOGFlNzRjOThhYmVhYTkxYWFlMDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/c492ba22f3cfab47ddd322b51e6d8481baf4053f","sha":"c492ba22f3cfab47ddd322b51e6d8481baf4053f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/c492ba22f3cfab47ddd322b51e6d8481baf4053f"}],"sha":"6061f26804a09e09db508ae74c98abeaa91aae02","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/6061f26804a09e09db508ae74c98abeaa91aae02"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/c492ba22f3cfab47ddd322b51e6d8481baf4053f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T01:43:55Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T01:43:55Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Add the UI Provenance Instrumenter: registry-backed element identity\n\nA line number is not an identity. Neither is a CSS selector, a DOM index or a\nReact internal: all four change under ordinary work, and an anchor that moves\nwhen a file is reformatted is worse than no anchor.\n\nSo identity is assigned once and recorded in a source-controlled registry.\n`ui-provenance sync` resolves each JSX element against it in a fixed order -\nexplicit key, exact match, one unique structural match in the component, one\nunique move or rename, then a new id - and fails with UIP_AMBIGUOUS_IDENTITY\nrather than guessing when two prior identities are equally plausible.\n\nThe fingerprint deliberately excludes line, column, whitespace, class names,\nprop order and sibling shapes. Every one of them changes under work a developer\ndoes without thinking, and the last of them would perturb every neighbour at\nonce when an unrelated sibling is added.\n\nWhere several candidates are genuinely indistinguishable - two sibling lists\nwhose only difference is a class name - position decides, by slot among\nsame-type siblings before file index, and only among candidates that already\nmatched on everything else. Both rules came out of the golden evaluation\ncatching the alternative in the act.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"9a15c74f3141f7fd198b6e0a6dffcac59c230cdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/9a15c74f3141f7fd198b6e0a6dffcac59c230cdc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/c492ba22f3cfab47ddd322b51e6d8481baf4053f","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a15c74f3141f7fd198b6e0a6dffcac59c230cdc\nparent 6a83bc7b98f9cfb9d14214424b09cba2665c0e2e\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789177435 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789177435 +0000\n\nAdd the UI Provenance Instrumenter: registry-backed element identity\n\nA line number is not an identity. Neither is a CSS selector, a DOM index or a\nReact internal: all four change under ordinary work, and an anchor that moves\nwhen a file is reformatted is worse than no anchor.\n\nSo identity is assigned once and recorded in a source-controlled registry.\n`ui-provenance sync` resolves each JSX element against it in a fixed order -\nexplicit key, exact match, one unique structural match in the component, one\nunique move or rename, then a new id - and fails with UIP_AMBIGUOUS_IDENTITY\nrather than guessing when two prior identities are equally plausible.\n\nThe fingerprint deliberately excludes line, column, whitespace, class names,\nprop order and sibling shapes. Every one of them changes under work a developer\ndoes without thinking, and the last of them would perturb every neighbour at\nonce when an unrelated sibling is added.\n\nWhere several candidates are genuinely indistinguishable - two sibling lists\nwhose only difference is a class name - position decides, by slot among\nsame-type siblings before file index, and only among candidates that already\nmatched on everything else. Both rules came out of the golden evaluation\ncatching the alternative in the act.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOiyY1up\nG7lIB5JOoH1YVeNlEFmWgstW61rd0K8/I659zLyM1xPjaugb246PQOiGWIycK/VD9D6gondePBfb\nwgk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/c492ba22f3cfab47ddd322b51e6d8481baf4053f","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKGM0OTJiYTIyZjNjZmFiNDdkZGQzMjJiNTFlNmQ4NDgxYmFmNDA1M2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/6a83bc7b98f9cfb9d14214424b09cba2665c0e2e","sha":"6a83bc7b98f9cfb9d14214424b09cba2665c0e2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/6a83bc7b98f9cfb9d14214424b09cba2665c0e2e"}],"sha":"c492ba22f3cfab47ddd322b51e6d8481baf4053f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/c492ba22f3cfab47ddd322b51e6d8481baf4053f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/6a83bc7b98f9cfb9d14214424b09cba2665c0e2e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:46:49Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:46:49Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Document the toolbar, federation and what is not shipped\n\nThe reframe in prose: an embeddable review toolbar and its anchoring SDK, not a\ndesign-system library and not an application. Adds the embedding guide, the\nfederation half of the provenance contract, and the two rules that came out of\nrunning it in a browser - discounting a semantic match that contradicts the\nnode''s own identity, and metering one re-anchor pass per build.\n\nStates plainly that the API is not shipped, and that the repository interface is\nwhere it lands.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"35d22a277db9d210054c7c9d58314d718d468878","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/35d22a277db9d210054c7c9d58314d718d468878"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/6a83bc7b98f9cfb9d14214424b09cba2665c0e2e","verification":{"payload":"tree 35d22a277db9d210054c7c9d58314d718d468878\nparent 3a85b3e2af10bfa680ce9dd05b453f30d14cb6b8\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789174009 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789174009 +0000\n\nDocument the toolbar, federation and what is not shipped\n\nThe reframe in prose: an embeddable review toolbar and its anchoring SDK, not a\ndesign-system library and not an application. Adds the embedding guide, the\nfederation half of the provenance contract, and the two rules that came out of\nrunning it in a browser - discounting a semantic match that contradicts the\nnode''s own identity, and metering one re-anchor pass per build.\n\nStates plainly that the API is not shipped, and that the repository interface is\nwhere it lands.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQE+7Z2qz\ni7P1FbC3JkgBdVHmzv+DMVfDQqT6rucqJ1dxkFVu7GoAiyJaNP6MExfYIS7SNLKrLRb9ZvXyUBBg\nAgg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/6a83bc7b98f9cfb9d14214424b09cba2665c0e2e","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDZhODNiYzdiOThmOWNmYjlkMTQyMTQ0MjRiMDljYmEyNjY1YzBlMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/3a85b3e2af10bfa680ce9dd05b453f30d14cb6b8","sha":"3a85b3e2af10bfa680ce9dd05b453f30d14cb6b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/3a85b3e2af10bfa680ce9dd05b453f30d14cb6b8"}],"sha":"6a83bc7b98f9cfb9d14214424b09cba2665c0e2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/6a83bc7b98f9cfb9d14214424b09cba2665c0e2e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/3a85b3e2af10bfa680ce9dd05b453f30d14cb6b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:46:49Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:46:49Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Replace the demo with a federated shell and two remotes\n\nA single-bundle demo could not test the thing that actually breaks anchors:\nseparate builds, separate origins, lazy loading, and a version pinned per\nremote. The shell is a Module Federation 2 host; payments-dash and limits-panel\nare remotes with their own instrumentation, their own manifests and their own\nmock services.\n\nSwitching to build B loads a different federated module - the same components\nafter a refactor - so a rebuild is something you watch happen rather than\nsomething the fixtures assert. Shell and MFEs are built with Salt, and the\ntoken bindings on each node are the real Salt custom properties, so a token-level\nanchor is checkable against the running theme.\n\nThe browser suite now covers the federation boundary, the crop on an orphaned\nthread, and threads surviving a reload. It earned its keep again: the settle\ntiming and the sibling-matching bug both came out of running it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"548aa24b73e66d9cdc79b8bc024f2ee9691175f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/548aa24b73e66d9cdc79b8bc024f2ee9691175f0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/3a85b3e2af10bfa680ce9dd05b453f30d14cb6b8","verification":{"payload":"tree 548aa24b73e66d9cdc79b8bc024f2ee9691175f0\nparent 00f05eee263611b6b86f78c9a8916a17a0d45834\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789174009 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789174009 +0000\n\nReplace the demo with a federated shell and two remotes\n\nA single-bundle demo could not test the thing that actually breaks anchors:\nseparate builds, separate origins, lazy loading, and a version pinned per\nremote. The shell is a Module Federation 2 host; payments-dash and limits-panel\nare remotes with their own instrumentation, their own manifests and their own\nmock services.\n\nSwitching to build B loads a different federated module - the same components\nafter a refactor - so a rebuild is something you watch happen rather than\nsomething the fixtures assert. Shell and MFEs are built with Salt, and the\ntoken bindings on each node are the real Salt custom properties, so a token-level\nanchor is checkable against the running theme.\n\nThe browser suite now covers the federation boundary, the crop on an orphaned\nthread, and threads surviving a reload. It earned its keep again: the settle\ntiming and the sibling-matching bug both came out of running it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJtGDCZ6\n6NObipT2UKpqk+PxJO+2teJpvlFOP4mKl2aoFzlgXF7UUbCEqPtG9aA5dxiMRPG1dOy1H14USAHP\nKAg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/3a85b3e2af10bfa680ce9dd05b453f30d14cb6b8","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDNhODViM2UyYWYxMGJmYTY4MGNlOWRkMDViNDUzZjMwZDE0Y2I2Yjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/00f05eee263611b6b86f78c9a8916a17a0d45834","sha":"00f05eee263611b6b86f78c9a8916a17a0d45834","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/00f05eee263611b6b86f78c9a8916a17a0d45834"}],"sha":"3a85b3e2af10bfa680ce9dd05b453f30d14cb6b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/3a85b3e2af10bfa680ce9dd05b453f30d14cb6b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/00f05eee263611b6b86f78c9a8916a17a0d45834/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:46:49Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:46:49Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Turn the feedback UI into a toolbar the Frame mounts\n\nPhase 1 is an embeddable preview-review surface, not a component library. So the\nentry point is now mountFeedbackToolbar(): the Frame mounts it into a preview,\nand the MFEs below are not modified, do not import it, and do not know it is\nthere. That is what makes it usable over an MFE the reviewer''s team does not own.\n\nBuilt with Salt, so the toolbar follows whatever theme the Frame is running. It\nis not in a shadow root: Salt injects component CSS into the document at runtime\nand cannot target one in this version, so a shadow root would leave every\ncomponent unstyled. The trade is written down in docs/embedding.md.\n\nRe-anchoring now waits for the preview DOM to go quiet before the metered pass.\nA federated preview does not arrive at once - remotes resolve lazily, data lands\nafter them - and measuring at the instant the pinned inputs change reported a\nhalf-rendered page as entirely orphaned. Passes driven by later DOM churn keep\npins attached but are not metered, so the orphan rate stays one honest number\nper build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"0a55358a1f1cad1872841f2f8178e5ba3b85d0fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/0a55358a1f1cad1872841f2f8178e5ba3b85d0fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/00f05eee263611b6b86f78c9a8916a17a0d45834","verification":{"payload":"tree 0a55358a1f1cad1872841f2f8178e5ba3b85d0fc\nparent 726ee3569c5e87ac6177e1e72f10a4d52c5857a5\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789174009 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789174009 +0000\n\nTurn the feedback UI into a toolbar the Frame mounts\n\nPhase 1 is an embeddable preview-review surface, not a component library. So the\nentry point is now mountFeedbackToolbar(): the Frame mounts it into a preview,\nand the MFEs below are not modified, do not import it, and do not know it is\nthere. That is what makes it usable over an MFE the reviewer''s team does not own.\n\nBuilt with Salt, so the toolbar follows whatever theme the Frame is running. It\nis not in a shadow root: Salt injects component CSS into the document at runtime\nand cannot target one in this version, so a shadow root would leave every\ncomponent unstyled. The trade is written down in docs/embedding.md.\n\nRe-anchoring now waits for the preview DOM to go quiet before the metered pass.\nA federated preview does not arrive at once - remotes resolve lazily, data lands\nafter them - and measuring at the instant the pinned inputs change reported a\nhalf-rendered page as entirely orphaned. Passes driven by later DOM churn keep\npins attached but are not metered, so the orphan rate stays one honest number\nper build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJiAhWEF\nQzmLXwstMz/ZKn2ZOHBGVLRCFUb17cwAEGKP0+XuyQiRf3hktm4RDUJcIhzEXLR6Ty6vt4tX+Dnv\nUwc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/00f05eee263611b6b86f78c9a8916a17a0d45834","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDAwZjA1ZWVlMjYzNjExYjZiODZmNzhjOWE4OTE2YTE3YTBkNDU4MzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/726ee3569c5e87ac6177e1e72f10a4d52c5857a5","sha":"726ee3569c5e87ac6177e1e72f10a4d52c5857a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/726ee3569c5e87ac6177e1e72f10a4d52c5857a5"}],"sha":"00f05eee263611b6b86f78c9a8916a17a0d45834","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/00f05eee263611b6b86f78c9a8916a17a0d45834"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/726ee3569c5e87ac6177e1e72f10a4d52c5857a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:46:49Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:46:49Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Add the datastore model for threads, users and preview versions\n\nOne repository interface, two local implementations, and no service. The HTTP\nimplementation is the next piece of work; nothing above the interface knows\nwhich implementation it has.\n\nTwo details the model has to get right. A resolution holds a live DOM element\nthat belongs to a build which no longer exists, so it is dropped on write and\nrestored as null on read rather than serialised or thrown over. And preview\nversions are stored, not just the current lock: without that history a thread\nwritten three versions ago can report that it is stale but never what moved.\n\nPersistence is also why a reviewer can reload a preview mid-thread and still be\nin it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"c2abff89ece25f41fb4f6994d4454c81e14ca596","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/c2abff89ece25f41fb4f6994d4454c81e14ca596"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/726ee3569c5e87ac6177e1e72f10a4d52c5857a5","verification":{"payload":"tree c2abff89ece25f41fb4f6994d4454c81e14ca596\nparent ed07411ccf1ac4f9fc87caaa7e2a0c1b8aa2b323\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789174009 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789174009 +0000\n\nAdd the datastore model for threads, users and preview versions\n\nOne repository interface, two local implementations, and no service. The HTTP\nimplementation is the next piece of work; nothing above the interface knows\nwhich implementation it has.\n\nTwo details the model has to get right. A resolution holds a live DOM element\nthat belongs to a build which no longer exists, so it is dropped on write and\nrestored as null on read rather than serialised or thrown over. And preview\nversions are stored, not just the current lock: without that history a thread\nwritten three versions ago can report that it is stale but never what moved.\n\nPersistence is also why a reviewer can reload a preview mid-thread and still be\nin it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBYlH+Im\nzaYlcZ42k4hhYlFTH0bikZdT+60KbvsZELo6uOkXngLfn3Ag361UxtvhXcxtWDCLWdihw0yVzaw3\nWwQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/726ee3569c5e87ac6177e1e72f10a4d52c5857a5","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDcyNmVlMzU2OWM1ZTg3YWM2MTc3ZTFlNzJmMTBhNGQ1MmM1ODU3YTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/ed07411ccf1ac4f9fc87caaa7e2a0c1b8aa2b323","sha":"ed07411ccf1ac4f9fc87caaa7e2a0c1b8aa2b323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/ed07411ccf1ac4f9fc87caaa7e2a0c1b8aa2b323"}],"sha":"726ee3569c5e87ac6177e1e72f10a4d52c5857a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/726ee3569c5e87ac6177e1e72f10a4d52c5857a5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/ed07411ccf1ac4f9fc87caaa7e2a0c1b8aa2b323/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:46:24Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:46:24Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Capture a screenshot crop with every anchor\n\nAn orphan nobody recognises is an orphan nobody triages. The crop is what lets a\nthread whose anchor is in trouble still show the reviewer what the comment was\nabout.\n\nIt is triage evidence, never matching input: nothing in the resolution chain\nreads it. Rendering goes through an SVG foreignObject so it needs no dependency\nand no service, and every known failure - a tainted canvas, an element with no\narea, a host screenshot service that is down - returns no crop rather than\nthrowing. Losing it must never cost the comment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"958c7216495ec0d27192cbbcb513696aec148564","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/958c7216495ec0d27192cbbcb513696aec148564"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/ed07411ccf1ac4f9fc87caaa7e2a0c1b8aa2b323","verification":{"payload":"tree 958c7216495ec0d27192cbbcb513696aec148564\nparent 5f606a8ca8c087bc720a521528212602d161e89b\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789173984 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789173984 +0000\n\nCapture a screenshot crop with every anchor\n\nAn orphan nobody recognises is an orphan nobody triages. The crop is what lets a\nthread whose anchor is in trouble still show the reviewer what the comment was\nabout.\n\nIt is triage evidence, never matching input: nothing in the resolution chain\nreads it. Rendering goes through an SVG foreignObject so it needs no dependency\nand no service, and every known failure - a tainted canvas, an element with no\narea, a host screenshot service that is down - returns no crop rather than\nthrowing. Losing it must never cost the comment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMXYjsC8\nh9RdrrSExD9NgBIEqGZwI5gCJmn3kPdXE9mdb0q6x5ClldXWgSrJhygHhieMgALJgYonQ6SZ6YVW\n4wM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/ed07411ccf1ac4f9fc87caaa7e2a0c1b8aa2b323","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKGVkMDc0MTFjY2YxYWM0ZjlmYzg3Y2FhYTdlMmEwYzFiOGFhMmIzMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/5f606a8ca8c087bc720a521528212602d161e89b","sha":"5f606a8ca8c087bc720a521528212602d161e89b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/5f606a8ca8c087bc720a521528212602d161e89b"}],"sha":"ed07411ccf1ac4f9fc87caaa7e2a0c1b8aa2b323","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/ed07411ccf1ac4f9fc87caaa7e2a0c1b8aa2b323"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/5f606a8ca8c087bc720a521528212602d161e89b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:46:24Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:46:24Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Stop the semantic level matching a node''s sibling\n\nTwo plain divs inside one component share a semantic path exactly, so a path\nalone was enough to move a comment onto the wrong node with full confidence -\nthe failure this project cares most about avoiding. Watching it happen in a real\npreview is what surfaced it: a comment on a summary card silently reattached to\nthe header beside it.\n\nA candidate that contradicts what the node carries itself - its own text, its\ntoken bindings - is now discounted, so a full-path match lands as degraded with\nthe contradiction named and a partial one stops clearing the floor.\n\nCandidates are also selected by tag rather than from the provenance index. A\nnode rendered inside a design-system component carries no provenance of its own\nbut still sits on a path through the application component that placed it;\nselecting from the index made every such node unaddressable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"c453907a12bb5097f30e23db0bc30dbfafc0a507","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/c453907a12bb5097f30e23db0bc30dbfafc0a507"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/5f606a8ca8c087bc720a521528212602d161e89b","verification":{"payload":"tree c453907a12bb5097f30e23db0bc30dbfafc0a507\nparent 27c1f8d60d1d4f8dceb4f431f894f46dad1385cf\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789173984 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789173984 +0000\n\nStop the semantic level matching a node''s sibling\n\nTwo plain divs inside one component share a semantic path exactly, so a path\nalone was enough to move a comment onto the wrong node with full confidence -\nthe failure this project cares most about avoiding. Watching it happen in a real\npreview is what surfaced it: a comment on a summary card silently reattached to\nthe header beside it.\n\nA candidate that contradicts what the node carries itself - its own text, its\ntoken bindings - is now discounted, so a full-path match lands as degraded with\nthe contradiction named and a partial one stops clearing the floor.\n\nCandidates are also selected by tag rather than from the provenance index. A\nnode rendered inside a design-system component carries no provenance of its own\nbut still sits on a path through the application component that placed it;\nselecting from the index made every such node unaddressable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCb26vRB\nSLOlp6hBjCOwJ1LUQQ5Fax6NKz6u+jyHK4k6radf1NN+oNDJdet5FuERR/OkgSMxAW0kT9COY/Nt\nrww=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/5f606a8ca8c087bc720a521528212602d161e89b","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDVmNjA2YThjYThjMDg3YmM3MjBhNTIxNTI4MjEyNjAyZDE2MWU4OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/27c1f8d60d1d4f8dceb4f431f894f46dad1385cf","sha":"27c1f8d60d1d4f8dceb4f431f894f46dad1385cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/27c1f8d60d1d4f8dceb4f431f894f46dad1385cf"}],"sha":"5f606a8ca8c087bc720a521528212602d161e89b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/5f606a8ca8c087bc720a521528212602d161e89b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/27c1f8d60d1d4f8dceb4f431f894f46dad1385cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:46:24Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:46:24Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Scope provenance manifests to federated participants\n\nUnder Module Federation there is no single repo or commit for a page: each\nremote is built by its own pipeline, at its own commit, and publishes its own\nmanifest. One repo/commit pair at the top of the manifest was a single-build\nassumption that federation breaks.\n\nManifests are now keyed by scope, module ids are hashed with their scope so two\nremotes shipping the same path cannot collide, and the shell merges every\nparticipant''s manifest into the view the anchor index resolves against. A\nprovenance reference carries the scope that built it, so a file and line can be\nread against the right commit.\n\nThe published files are also served cross-origin by default. A shell reads its\nremotes'' manifests from their own origins; these are build metadata for a\npreview, not application data.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"43bc39580d5d9e46a8df8daae4eedfda0a68c1f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/43bc39580d5d9e46a8df8daae4eedfda0a68c1f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/27c1f8d60d1d4f8dceb4f431f894f46dad1385cf","verification":{"payload":"tree 43bc39580d5d9e46a8df8daae4eedfda0a68c1f2\nparent cacd83e18048cc02ab178c41d3a02228d5f39b17\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789173984 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789173984 +0000\n\nScope provenance manifests to federated participants\n\nUnder Module Federation there is no single repo or commit for a page: each\nremote is built by its own pipeline, at its own commit, and publishes its own\nmanifest. One repo/commit pair at the top of the manifest was a single-build\nassumption that federation breaks.\n\nManifests are now keyed by scope, module ids are hashed with their scope so two\nremotes shipping the same path cannot collide, and the shell merges every\nparticipant''s manifest into the view the anchor index resolves against. A\nprovenance reference carries the scope that built it, so a file and line can be\nread against the right commit.\n\nThe published files are also served cross-origin by default. A shell reads its\nremotes'' manifests from their own origins; these are build metadata for a\npreview, not application data.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHF46St2\nS5kiBmSv/ZXP45gk1Qk7FwYwaH0HdbSH0mJwSnBAmwA546yR5Eblsto1mAAV8GP2/cW9k1AIjjIe\nrAM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/27c1f8d60d1d4f8dceb4f431f894f46dad1385cf","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDI3YzFmOGQ2MGQxZDRmOGRjZWI0ZjQzMWY4OTRmNDZkYWQxMzg1Y2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/cacd83e18048cc02ab178c41d3a02228d5f39b17","sha":"cacd83e18048cc02ab178c41d3a02228d5f39b17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/cacd83e18048cc02ab178c41d3a02228d5f39b17"}],"sha":"27c1f8d60d1d4f8dceb4f431f894f46dad1385cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/27c1f8d60d1d4f8dceb4f431f894f46dad1385cf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/cacd83e18048cc02ab178c41d3a02228d5f39b17/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:04:15Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:04:15Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Document the provenance contract and the resolution chain\n\nWhat each level survives, what it costs, and the three matches that are refused\non purpose. Also what phase 1 deliberately does not build, and the three things\nit carries anyway because retrofitting them is expensive: a named owner per\nthread, the context lock on every anchor, and per-build orphan history.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"a3209d50fc79525e92aa9cbea54959674eb84fa2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/a3209d50fc79525e92aa9cbea54959674eb84fa2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/cacd83e18048cc02ab178c41d3a02228d5f39b17","verification":{"payload":"tree a3209d50fc79525e92aa9cbea54959674eb84fa2\nparent 93588fdeeec30939a8466c9b759c0006131eab81\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789171455 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789171455 +0000\n\nDocument the provenance contract and the resolution chain\n\nWhat each level survives, what it costs, and the three matches that are refused\non purpose. Also what phase 1 deliberately does not build, and the three things\nit carries anyway because retrofitting them is expensive: a named owner per\nthread, the context lock on every anchor, and per-build orphan history.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFO784oT\nzCKjl+f7lIHp+3tod+EG1i7aT68aHrDGJF8bhBePLRyqOJlPYKswh+jlq3JjQrqWcjexDpHD2c6w\nSAk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/cacd83e18048cc02ab178c41d3a02228d5f39b17","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKGNhY2Q4M2UxODA0OGNjMDJhYjE3OGM0MWQzYTAyMjI4ZDVmMzliMTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/93588fdeeec30939a8466c9b759c0006131eab81","sha":"93588fdeeec30939a8466c9b759c0006131eab81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/93588fdeeec30939a8466c9b759c0006131eab81"}],"sha":"cacd83e18048cc02ab178c41d3a02228d5f39b17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/cacd83e18048cc02ab178c41d3a02228d5f39b17"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/93588fdeeec30939a8466c9b759c0006131eab81/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:04:15Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:04:15Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Add the pinned preview demo and a browser proof of the loop\n\nOne Frame, two MFEs, entitlement-shaped runtime events and mock data good enough\nthat reviewers comment on the UI rather than on the data. Build B is the same\npayments MFE after a refactor: components moved to a new file, markup\nrestructured, the summary card deleted, the version bumped.\n\nSwitching builds shows the three outcomes rather than asserting them. The badge\ncomment holds at the provenance level through its authored instance key and is\nmarked degraded. The network comment is untouched. The comment on the deleted\ncard orphans, and says what the chain tried.\n\nThe Playwright suite runs that walkthrough in a real browser. It is opt-in and\nnot part of pnpm test, but it is the only place the visual level of the chain\ncan be exercised: jsdom reports every box as zero. It earned its keep by\ncatching two defects - semantic paths that carried the app shell above the Frame\nboundary, and a visual match that accepted a different tag.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"d6d11fc2a25df6252d48258a4d13e4bfcb2fae3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/d6d11fc2a25df6252d48258a4d13e4bfcb2fae3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/93588fdeeec30939a8466c9b759c0006131eab81","verification":{"payload":"tree d6d11fc2a25df6252d48258a4d13e4bfcb2fae3f\nparent 2ead9e9a0625e46251ae3266078408e0ce6dcf00\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789171455 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789171455 +0000\n\nAdd the pinned preview demo and a browser proof of the loop\n\nOne Frame, two MFEs, entitlement-shaped runtime events and mock data good enough\nthat reviewers comment on the UI rather than on the data. Build B is the same\npayments MFE after a refactor: components moved to a new file, markup\nrestructured, the summary card deleted, the version bumped.\n\nSwitching builds shows the three outcomes rather than asserting them. The badge\ncomment holds at the provenance level through its authored instance key and is\nmarked degraded. The network comment is untouched. The comment on the deleted\ncard orphans, and says what the chain tried.\n\nThe Playwright suite runs that walkthrough in a real browser. It is opt-in and\nnot part of pnpm test, but it is the only place the visual level of the chain\ncan be exercised: jsdom reports every box as zero. It earned its keep by\ncatching two defects - semantic paths that carried the app shell above the Frame\nboundary, and a visual match that accepted a different tag.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFDuNCnz\nDof4o9uqAOqAsvD0gTkq9sY98oLcTBmVLMfqRPKgEsFR9Sy34aRVUBCZK1YoVAEq3aXj0T76ms2l\nNQ0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/93588fdeeec30939a8466c9b759c0006131eab81","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDkzNTg4ZmRlZWVjMzA5MzlhODQ2NmM5Yjc1OWMwMDA2MTMxZWFiODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/2ead9e9a0625e46251ae3266078408e0ce6dcf00","sha":"2ead9e9a0625e46251ae3266078408e0ce6dcf00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/2ead9e9a0625e46251ae3266078408e0ce6dcf00"}],"sha":"93588fdeeec30939a8466c9b759c0006131eab81","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/93588fdeeec30939a8466c9b759c0006131eab81"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/2ead9e9a0625e46251ae3266078408e0ce6dcf00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:04:15Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:04:15Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Add the anchored feedback UI for pinned previews\n\nClick-to-anchor over a running preview, pins that carry their anchor status, and\na thread panel that shows how each comment held: which level is carrying it, at\nwhat confidence, and for an orphan, what the chain tried.\n\nThe overlay marks its own DOM so the anchor index skips it - a comment must\nnever anchor to the commenting tool - and a pick is swallowed before the preview\napp can treat it as a real click.\n\nDeveloper feedback targets things that are not on screen, so the instrumented\npanel records network calls, the runtime events a Frame declares, and the build\nreport. Those anchor by their own payload and travel through the same thread\nmachinery as a spacing correction: one model, five anchor types.\n\nThe provider re-anchors the open set whenever the pinned inputs move. A rebuild\nthat does not re-anchor is how comments go missing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"7db3e428da601813ec653952207251d9f53d068b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/7db3e428da601813ec653952207251d9f53d068b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/2ead9e9a0625e46251ae3266078408e0ce6dcf00","verification":{"payload":"tree 7db3e428da601813ec653952207251d9f53d068b\nparent ca5b02df09fbdcd61cf6f6b27668785a3786f7ae\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789171455 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789171455 +0000\n\nAdd the anchored feedback UI for pinned previews\n\nClick-to-anchor over a running preview, pins that carry their anchor status, and\na thread panel that shows how each comment held: which level is carrying it, at\nwhat confidence, and for an orphan, what the chain tried.\n\nThe overlay marks its own DOM so the anchor index skips it - a comment must\nnever anchor to the commenting tool - and a pick is swallowed before the preview\napp can treat it as a real click.\n\nDeveloper feedback targets things that are not on screen, so the instrumented\npanel records network calls, the runtime events a Frame declares, and the build\nreport. Those anchor by their own payload and travel through the same thread\nmachinery as a spacing correction: one model, five anchor types.\n\nThe provider re-anchors the open set whenever the pinned inputs move. A rebuild\nthat does not re-anchor is how comments go missing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQME2Rf1F\n4jrfVhEqgBQx0OYRVjQaPbjen1ZWSrJycqWHOZ0Un70r5zz8hbIiTHIwFiLIID2wvyneO4pukYOO\nLQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/2ead9e9a0625e46251ae3266078408e0ce6dcf00","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKDJlYWQ5ZTlhMDYyNWU0NjI1MWFlMzI2NjA3ODQwOGUwY2U2ZGNmMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/ca5b02df09fbdcd61cf6f6b27668785a3786f7ae","sha":"ca5b02df09fbdcd61cf6f6b27668785a3786f7ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/ca5b02df09fbdcd61cf6f6b27668785a3786f7ae"}],"sha":"2ead9e9a0625e46251ae3266078408e0ce6dcf00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/2ead9e9a0625e46251ae3266078408e0ce6dcf00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/ca5b02df09fbdcd61cf6f6b27668785a3786f7ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:04:14Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:04:14Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Add build-time provenance instrumentation\n\nNothing at runtime can reconstruct which component, in which file, produced a\ngiven DOM node, so the build emits it.\n\nThe babel plugin marks host elements with a compact \"<module>:<line>:<column>\"\ntoken and records the rest in a manifest, keeping the DOM cost to a dozen bytes\nper node. Component elements are left alone: an attribute on a component is a\nprop, and props do not reliably reach the DOM. Elements are attributed to the\nnearest component-shaped enclosing name, walking up through render helpers.\n\nThe bundler plugin publishes the manifest, the context lock and a build report\nalongside the preview - served live in dev, emitted as assets in a build, with\nper-module invalidation so a hot update cannot leave a stale node behind.\n\nThis is additive: an MFE adds the plugin and nothing else about it changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"a87b8df9cce3ba063f5545117367441294dbab13","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/a87b8df9cce3ba063f5545117367441294dbab13"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/ca5b02df09fbdcd61cf6f6b27668785a3786f7ae","verification":{"payload":"tree a87b8df9cce3ba063f5545117367441294dbab13\nparent b117c869e4d152fcfdf8e7a87ae1f148e27b19f1\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789171454 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789171454 +0000\n\nAdd build-time provenance instrumentation\n\nNothing at runtime can reconstruct which component, in which file, produced a\ngiven DOM node, so the build emits it.\n\nThe babel plugin marks host elements with a compact \"<module>:<line>:<column>\"\ntoken and records the rest in a manifest, keeping the DOM cost to a dozen bytes\nper node. Component elements are left alone: an attribute on a component is a\nprop, and props do not reliably reach the DOM. Elements are attributed to the\nnearest component-shaped enclosing name, walking up through render helpers.\n\nThe bundler plugin publishes the manifest, the context lock and a build report\nalongside the preview - served live in dev, emitted as assets in a build, with\nper-module invalidation so a hot update cannot leave a stale node behind.\n\nThis is additive: an MFE adds the plugin and nothing else about it changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJOcvnzc\nckCPU39O0Lvqhn/xx3OFnPDkeLL7QTJwNtJJ4W+vuqbDaQvnK81Bz7C6qW5D83EgNEKGt5ou6Pfo\nQw0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/ca5b02df09fbdcd61cf6f6b27668785a3786f7ae","node_id":"C_kwDOObgUgtoAKGNhNWIwMmRmMDlmYmRjZDYxY2Y2ZjZiMjc2Njg3ODVhMzc4NmY3YWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass/management-console/commit/b117c869e4d152fcfdf8e7a87ae1f148e27b19f1","sha":"b117c869e4d152fcfdf8e7a87ae1f148e27b19f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/b117c869e4d152fcfdf8e7a87ae1f148e27b19f1"}],"sha":"ca5b02df09fbdcd61cf6f6b27668785a3786f7ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/ca5b02df09fbdcd61cf6f6b27668785a3786f7ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/roughcompass","id":173234,"login":"roughcompass","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MzIzNA==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/commits/b117c869e4d152fcfdf8e7a87ae1f148e27b19f1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:04:14Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T00:04:14Z","email":"173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com","name":"roughcompass"},"message":"Add anchor core: context lock, capture, resolution chain, orphan meter\n\nThe four primitives phase 1 needs, with no framework dependency.\n\nA comment on a running MFE attaches to a DOM node, and that node will not exist\nin the same form after the next rebuild. So an anchor stores all five levels at\ncapture time - provenance id, semantic path, token references, text, visual box\n- and re-anchoring walks them in fixed order, taking the first level that clears\nits floor.\n\nThree matches are refused on purpose, because a wrong anchor is worse than a\nflagged orphan: a semantic path of nothing but a tag name, a visual box over a\ndifferent tag, and a visual box under a different theme or viewport.\n\nA match below the level it was captured at is reported as degraded rather than\nsilently accepted. A match nowhere is an orphan that records every level tried\nand why each failed.\n\nFeedbackStore runs the whole open set against a rebuild in one indexed pass and\nreturns that build''s orphan rate, degraded rate, confidence and per-level\ndistribution. Staleness is tracked separately from anchoring and reported as a\ndiff of the pinned inputs, never as a silent carry-forward.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k","tree":{"sha":"7e276d94b81817529452b96c5e9833070daeedc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/trees/7e276d94b81817529452b96c5e9833070daeedc8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/roughcompass/management-console/git/commits/b117c869e4d152fcfdf8e7a87ae1f148e27b19f1","verification":{"payload":"tree 7e276d94b81817529452b96c5e9833070daeedc8\nparent 5b47c6a24d1b2607cd3f5281c9532da3986a6c06\nauthor roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789171454 +0000\ncommitter roughcompass <173234+roughcompass@users.noreply.github.com> 1789171454 +0000\n\nAdd anchor core: context lock, capture, resolution chain, orphan meter\n\nThe four primitives phase 1 needs, with no framework dependency.\n\nA comment on a running MFE attaches to a DOM node, and that node will not exist\nin the same form after the next rebuild. So an anchor stores all five levels at\ncapture time - provenance id, semantic path, token references, text, visual box\n- and re-anchoring walks them in fixed order, taking the first level that clears\nits floor.\n\nThree matches are refused on purpose, because a wrong anchor is worse than a\nflagged orphan: a semantic path of nothing but a tag name, a visual box over a\ndifferent tag, and a visual box under a different theme or viewport.\n\nA match below the level it was captured at is reported as degraded rather than\nsilently accepted. A match nowhere is an orphan that records every level tried\nand why each failed.\n\nFeedbackStore runs the whole open set against a rebuild in one indexed pass and\nreturns that build''s orphan rate, degraded rate, confidence and per-level\ndistribution. Staleness is tracked separately from anchoring and reported as a\ndiff of the pinned inputs, never as a silent carry-forward.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QeC6jjhjoSXg3HpzXV7R8k\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGb8H+an\n8TZu8fWJJIvjUuRhLM68hUv8X5oT4RvOylQ0FiLhWDDuw4jxAKpaP4O+a9EjdhhbwdJJro8onOyv\neAU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/173234?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/roughcompass/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"ht