:"https://api.github.com/users/devin-ai-integration%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/devin-ai-integration%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erkinalp/4chan-go-rs/commits/9af218f899d06696d26acc4e6ffbc2844515706c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-08-16T15:34:28Z","email":"158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Devin AI"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-08-16T15:34:28Z","email":"158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Devin AI"},"message":"feat: implement user-based fixed-window rate limiting across backend services\n\n- Add user-based rate limiting middleware to Go file service and go-service\n- Implement user-based rate limiting in Rust media processor with JWT claims extraction\n- Add NestJS user rate limiter interceptor with Redis integration\n- Extract user information from JWT tokens (user_id, role, created_at)\n- Implement fixed-window blocking with user-specific window alignment\n- Add block extension for requests during blocked periods\n- Fall back to IP-based rate limiting for unauthenticated requests\n- Configure different rate limits per service:\n  - Go services: 50 requests/60s for users\n  - Rust services: 20 requests/60s for users\n  - NestJS services: 100 requests/60s for users\n- Add comprehensive test script for user-based rate limiting\n- Update documentation with user-based rate limiting details\n- Add environment configuration files for all services\n\nComplements existing IP-based gateway rate limiting for comprehensive protection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Erkin Alp Güney <erkinalp9035@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a34af04391c9a8a75b06786c8222e41de77842f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erkinalp/4chan-go-rs/git/trees/2a34af04391c9a8a75b06786c8222e41de77842f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/erkinalp/4chan-go-rs/git/commits/9af218f899d06696d26acc4e6ffbc2844515706c","verification":{